    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hi, I'm looking for some clarification on UK inheritance tax (IHT) regarding assets held in offshore trusts. If a deceased individual was a UK resident but held significant real estate in a non-resident trust, how is the valuation of those specific assets treated for the purpose of calculating the taxable estate? Also, are there any common pitfalls where assets might be overlooked during the initial filing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generally, if a UK resident held an interest in an offshore trust that owned UK real estate, that real estate would likely fall within the deceased's estate for IHT purposes, even if held by the trust. The value of these assets is typically included based on the deceased's beneficial interest or their rights in the trust structure. A common pitfall is failing to disclose the existence or the beneficial interest in complex offshore structures, which can lead to HMRC penalties.",
      "source": "target",
